Convert one container block into another by moving (and cascade-converting) its child cells, and convert a single-value block to/from a container region. `convertBlockType` now recognises a `fieldMappings` entry whose target field names a container region (`blocks_layout` or `object_list`, top-level or nested via a `data/items` path) and reshapes the region — each child converted to a type the target allows, transitively through the same converter — and a `region/type/field` path that bridges a scalar value and a region (expand a value into one child; collapse a region's children into one value, sharing convertValueContainer's mechanics). This makes e.g. tabs⇄steps⇄definitionList⇄accordion and value⇄container conversions work from "Convert to…", cells and content preserved.
